@vsm 1.2.1
@status active
// exp-token-grounding.spec.vsm — token savings of state-grounded RAG/MCP
// vs cold. author [O] 2026-07-20 w/ rmw3. Exploratory phase of
// METHODOLOGY_VITRINE.
// RULE: measure, ¬proclaim. The honest number is the pitch.
// A FAIR baseline, not a strawman.
// PH-11 migrate + PH-11-CLOSE (2026-08-09): rewritten dense to meet the
// density gate — prose ≤ 5% · w/l ≤ 5.0. Semantics preserved; compression
// is real (shorter phrasing), ¬ line-splitting.

experiment(exp-token-grounding) status=SPEC {

  hypothesis:
    "State-grounded context (RAG-onboard ∘ MCP-query) cuts tokens vs cold,
     WITHOUT correctness loss. H0: no significant difference, or a
     difference at correctness cost. Rejectable by construction."

  conditions:  // 3 legs; SAME model · SAME task · SAME initial state
    "C0 COLD: task + repo access only. No injection, no MCP;
     re-explores to anchor. FAIR baseline: competent tools, ¬crippled
     (negative control)."
    "C1 RAG (onboard): task + onboard digest — canonical state —
     up front. Front-load: all upfront, zero exploration."
    "C2 MCP (query): task + state-MCP tools. Lazy — queries only what
     the task needs; more round-trips when narrow."

  key_insight:  // TRADE-OFF, non-strict order — the credible pitch
    "C1 front-loads state: more up front, zero exploration.
     C2 is lazy: fewer if narrow, more round-trips.
     ⟹ C1 wins BROAD tasks · C2 wins NARROW tasks → TWO tasks run."
    "Honest result = 'when each helps', not 'ours is better'."

  tasks:  // fixed, representative, state-dependent
    "T_broad: 'Report the system state: active services, drift/orphans,
     last decision.'  → favours C1 (needs most state)."
    "T_narrow: 'Is service X consistent with the declared topology?
     Drift?'  → favours C2 (needs one slice)."

  metrics:  // per trial
    "input_tokens (the big lever) · output_tokens · total · tool_calls
     (round-trips) · wall-clock."
    "CORRECTNESS: scored vs ground truth. Savings with an INCORRECT
     answer = DQ. cost: if pricing differs."

  controls:  // rigour that makes the number defensible
    "1. SAME model in ALL 3 — isolates anchoring; tiers separate."
    "2. Fixed initial state: state.db + corpus, fresh."
    "3. n ≥ 5 trials per condition → mean ± dispersion. One number
       lies; LLM is stochastic."
    "4. FAIR baseline: never cripple C0 to inflate the delta.
       5. Prompt-caching: disable or account consistently — bias."
    "6. Corpus realistic-VSF vs controlled. Prefer controlled
       (small/reproducible) — numbers must reproduce."

  harness:
    "OpenCode is the harness (on n02; reports usage). Three configs:
     no-context / onboard-injected / MCP-attached. Read its token
     report. Runs in an LXC sandbox (108 test-sandbox), NEVER on WSL.
     Tools = this repo (versioned) — binary provenance R1a."

  phasing:  // starts NOW — C0 needs no tooling
    "A (now): define 2 tasks + fixed corpus + measure C0 (the
     cold anchor)."
    "B: once the onboard digest exists, run C1."
    "C: once the MCP is prototyped, run C2."
    "Design: C0/C1 tasks DEFINE the MCP queries (phase C informs the
     interface — experiment before interface)."

  deliverable:
    "Table: condition × task: tokens + correctness + trade-off. The
     honest number for vitrine. H0 retained → say so. Rigour
     > marketing."

  placement:
    "state-canon-mcp source → standalone repo, NEVER inside VSF repo
     (2026-07-27 stale copy removed — STATE-CANON-MCP-MIGRATION)."
    run: "sandbox LXC 108 · notebook on n02 · never WSL."

  owner: "Claude [O] (hypothesis + design) → DS [S] (run harness)."

// Phase C — the vitrine anchor (mcp_prototype gate). A+B run now;
// C waits on the tool. debt(EXP-TOKEN-PHASE-C, class=experiment,
// owner=DS, gate=mcp_prototype)
}

